  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "6c81c18b-1b80-4128-ba2a-276791879edb",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 251,
      "shortId": "295EW",
      "priority": 6,
      "shortName": "plugin-task-ui-2",
      "title": "plugin-task-ui-2 — Typed SwiftUI-style builder SDK",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "# Typed, SwiftUI-style builder SDK over `ViewNode`\n\nAn ergonomic authoring layer over the uniform node. Lives in **`heca-view`**, so a plugin can depend\non it — that crate has no dependencies but serde, which is the whole reason it exists.\n\n## ⚠️ The original one-line description was written before the vocabulary was corrected\n\nIt said `Column::new().gap(8).child(...)`. **`Column` is not a kind any more.** F003/P017/T006\nrenamed `WidgetKind::Column` → `VStack` and `Row` → `HStack`, and gave **`Row`** to grid-ui's real\nclickable, selectable widget. Builders must follow the corrected vocabulary or this SDK would\nreintroduce exactly the confusion that rename removed.\n\n## ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-27\n\n**1. A type per widget kind.** One builder struct per `WidgetKind`, so a method exists only where\nthe widget really has that property — `Label::new(\"x\").title(\"y\")` is a **compile error**, not a\nsilently-ignored prop. The shared `Layout`/`Visual` properties come from **one trait implemented for\nevery builder**, written once, because after F003/P017/T007 those apply to every kind generically.\nRejected: a single generic `node(Kind)` builder — less code, but a nonsense method still compiles.\n\nTarget shape:\n\n```rust\nuse heca_view::build::*;\n\nlet tree = VStack::new()\n    .gap(8)\n    .child(\n        Panel::new().title(\"CONTAINERS\").child(\n            Row::new()\n                .padding(6)\n                .on_press(Intent::new(\"docker.select\").arg(\"id\", \"web\"))\n                .child(Label::new(\"nginx\"))\n                .child(Badge::new(\"UP\")),\n        ),\n    )\n    .child(Separator::new())\n    .child(Input::new().placeholder(\"filter…\").name(\"q\"))\n    .into_node();\n```\n\n**2. Hand-written, with a drift guard — not generated.** A test in **`heca-view-realize`** (the one\ncrate depending on both `heca-view` and `heca-grid-ui`) walks `WidgetKind::ALL` against each widget's\n`PROP_NAMES` and fails when a builder is missing a property the widget exposes. Fails **closed**, like\n`heca-grid-ui/tests/prop_drift.rs`: a new property must reach the SDK unless someone names an\nexception and says why. `heca-view` keeps zero dependencies — the guard lives above it.\n\n---\n\n# 📋 INVENTORY — taken 2026-07-27 from the compiler, not from reading. DO NOT RE-DERIVE.\n\n**The guard needs no source parsing.** `PROP_NAMES` / `HOST_ONLY_BUILDERS` are **trait consts on\n`SetProp`** (`heca-grid-ui/src/prop.rs:68`), so `<Row as SetProp>::PROP_NAMES` is readable from any\ncrate above `heca-grid-ui`. That is how this list was produced (a throwaway test in\n`heca-view-realize/tests/`), and it is how the guard should read it — `prop_drift.rs` parses sources\nonly because it must catch builders that have *no* surface at all.\n\n## The shared half — every field is settable by name through `merge_style_half`\n\n**`Layout` (34):** align, align_self, direction, flex_grow, flex_shrink, gap, gap_spacing,\ngrid_cell, height, hidden, justify, justify_items, justify_self, margin, margin_bottom,\nmargin_left, margin_right, margin_top, max_height, max_width, min_height, min_width, pad_spacing_x,\npad_spacing_y, padding, padding_bottom, padding_left, padding_right, padding_top, padding_x,\npadding_y, size, size_explicit, width\n\n**`Visual` (6):** border, fill, font_scale, font_size, glow, radius\n\n### Findings the Style trait has to deal with\n\n- **`width`/`height`/`min_*`/`max_*` are `Length`**, whose wire form is: a **number** → px, the\n  string **`\"auto\"`**, or a string like **`\"50%\"`** (`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs:141` — custom\n  Serialize/Deserialize). So the typed setters are `.width(240)`, `.width_pct(0.5)`,\n  `.width_auto()`, and there is no need for a `Length` mirror in the model.\n- **`border` and `glow` CANNOT be authored today.** They are structs (`Border{color,width}`,\n  `Glow{color,radius,intensity}`) and **`PropValue` has no map/object variant** — only Bool, Int,\n  Float, Text, Size, Variant, Align, Color, Glyph, List. So they are exceptions with a real reason,\n  not an oversight. (`fill` and `radius` *are* proven authorable — tests at\n  `heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs:1301` and `:1370`.) If they should become authorable, that is a\n  `PropValue` change and its own task.\n- **Do not expose:** `size_explicit` (set by the layout pass, not an author), `direction` (the kind\n  already says it — `HStack` with `direction: column` is a contradiction), `grid_cell` (Grid\n  placement is authored as `area`/`col`/`row` props read by the Grid arm), `pad_spacing_*` /\n  `gap_spacing` (theme `Spacing` tokens, no model mirror — see the open question).\n\n## The per-kind half — `PROP_NAMES` with real parameter types\n\n| Widget | Properties (type) |\n|---|---|\n| Alert | variant(`AlertVariant`), body(String) |\n| Badge | variant(`BadgeVariant`) |\n| BadgeButton | variant(`BadgeVariant`) |\n| Button | icon(`Glyph`), variant(`ButtonVariant`), font_size(f32), glow(bool), bordered(bool) |\n| Checkbox | checked(bool), label(String), label_side(`LabelSide`) |\n| Choice | selected(bool) |\n| DockFrame | frameless(bool), expanded(bool), active(bool), nav_selected(bool) |\n| Gauge | value(f32) |\n| Icon | size(f32), color(`Color`), secondary_color(`Color`), glow(bool) |\n| IconButton | cell(f32), tone(`Color`), glow(bool), active(bool) |\n| Input | font_size(f32), value(String), placeholder(String) |\n| Item | font_size(f32), active(bool), marker(`ActiveMarker`), muted(bool), leading_bordered(bool), trailing_bordered(bool) |\n| ItemGroup | expanded(bool) |\n| Label | align(`TextAlign`), color(`Color`), bold, italic, underline, strikethrough (bool), font_size(f32), font_scale(f32) |\n| MarkerGroup | active(bool), nav_selected(bool) |\n| Panel | title(String) |\n| RailCell | cell_size(f32), active(bool) |\n| Row | highlight(`Color`), attention_color(`Color`), active(bool), marker(`ActiveMarker`), nav_selected(bool) |\n| ScrollRegion | axes(`ScrollAxes`) |\n| Select | font_size(f32), selected(usize) |\n| Separator | orientation(`Orientation`), length(f32) |\n| Tabs | font_size(f32), selected(usize) |\n| Tag | color(`Color`) |\n| Toast | severity(`ToastSeverity`), icon(`Glyph`), body(String), dismissible(bool) |\n| Toggle | on(bool) |\n\n**`Card` and `StatusDot` do not implement `SetProp` at all** — no kind-specific properties; their\nbuilders are the shared trait plus (for Card) children.\n\nKinds whose widget is on `prop_drift`'s `NO_SURFACE_REQUIRED` list also have none: VStack/HStack\n(`Flex`), Surface, Grid, ScrollBar (host-only).\n\n## Events, per kind — only the ones `realize` actually reads\n\n- **press:** Row, Button, IconButton, BadgeButton, Item, RailCell, Choice\n- **change:** Input, Toggle, Checkbox, Select, Tabs\n- **toggle:** ItemGroup, DockFrame\n- **action + dismiss:** Toast\n\nA builder should expose only its own events, on the same principle as its properties. Note the\ncompiler cannot catch a wrong event *name* (it is a string in the model), so this mapping wants a\ntest: build through the SDK, realize, dispatch, assert the intent fires.\n\n## Which kinds take children\n\nVStack, HStack, Row, Grid, Card, Scroll, Panel, Surface, ItemGroup, DockFrame, MarkerGroup, Tabs,\nSelect (its options are `Choice` children), Choice, Button (its content is its children), Item\n(slots). **Toast takes none** — asserted by an existing test. Leaves: Label, Badge, Tag, Icon,\nInput, Toggle, Checkbox, StatusDot, Gauge, Separator, RailCell, Alert, ScrollBar.\n\n---\n\n# ❓ OPEN SUB-QUESTION — put to the user before writing the builders\n\n**Six enum-valued properties have no mirror in `heca-view`:** `ActiveMarker` (Row, Item),\n`ScrollAxes` (Scroll), `Orientation` (Separator), `LabelSide` (Checkbox), `ToastSeverity` (Toast),\n`AlertVariant` (Alert) — plus `TextAlign` (Label) and `Glyph` (Button/Toast/Icon).\n\nThey travel as **their name in snake_case** (the model's own rule; `PropInput::Text(prop_enum_name(..))`).\nSo a typed builder either:\n\n- **(a)** takes `&str` for these — no new model types, but `Separator::new().orientation(\"vertcal\")`\n  compiles and silently does nothing, which is the class of defect F003/P010/T006 spent a whole\n  task removing from actions; or\n- **(b)** adds mirror enums to `heca-view` alongside the existing `ViewVariant` / `ViewAlign` /\n  `ViewSize` — genuinely typed, at the cost of ~6 small enums and a mapping each in `realize`\n  (the mapping may already exist there: check, since props currently arrive as text).\n\n**(b) looks right** and matches why `ViewVariant`/`ViewAlign`/`ViewSize` exist at all, but it widens\nthe task and the user has NOT been asked yet. Do not pick it alone.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `heca-view::build` with a builder per `WidgetKind`, and the shared style trait written once.\n- A nonsense property is a compile error; the doc examples show that.\n- The drift guard fails closed against `PROP_NAMES`, every exception carrying a reason.\n- `heca-view` still depends on nothing but serde.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.\n- The showcase's described tree is rewritten through the builders — it is the one place a described\n  tree is visible, so it is also the proof the SDK is usable. **The user looks at it**; green tests\n  are not verification for anything visual.\n\n## State as of 2026-07-27\n\nTask is **in-progress**: decisions taken, inventory complete, **no code written yet**. Next action\nis the open sub-question above, then `heca-view/src/build.rs`.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n# ✅ DONE 2026-07-28 — `7183250`, verified in the app by the user\n\n`heca-view::build`: one builder type per `WidgetKind`, so a method exists only where the widget really\nhas that property. `Label::new(\"x\").title(\"y\")` does not compile; a `Toast` cannot be given children.\nShared arrangement and appearance setters live on one `Style` trait (written once, since both halves\nmerge generically for every kind); children on `Parent`, implemented only for the kinds `realize`\nattaches them to.\n\n`border` and `glow` are in it, which is only true because F003/P011/T018 landed first — otherwise the\nSDK would have shipped an exceptions list saying appearance is partly unreachable, freezing that hole\ninto a compile-checked API. That is why this task was split out of the phase in July.\n\n**The guard is the point, not the builders.** `every_widget_property_is_reachable_from_the_sdk`\n(`heca-view-realize`) walks each widget's generated `PROP_NAMES` and fails when a property has no\nsetter. It fails closed, and it bites — verified by deleting `Toast::dismissible` and reading the\nfailure. The seven exceptions are all `font_size`/`font_scale`, which `Style` already covers.\n\nAlso added here: `ViewJustify` — T019's inventory came from the widgets' own properties, and `justify`\nis a `Layout` field, so it never appeared.\n\n**Verified by the user 2026-07-28:** the showcase's described tree is written through the builders and\nrenders identically to the native panel beside it (\"ok they are the same\"). `WidgetKind` is no longer\nimported in the showcase — with the builders, nothing needs to name a kind.\n\nFollow-up recorded elsewhere: expressing a share via a fixed `height = Px(0)` is debt\n(F004/P006/T010), and the SDK's `flex_grow` setter has the same trap until that lands.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "6c81c18b-1b80-4128-ba2a-276791879edb-check-001-in-progress-planned",
          "date": "2026-07-25T19:16:30.000Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "planned",
          "title": "Back to planned 2026-07-25: started this session, then split. The research it triggered found that the declarative model cannot express padding, an input placeholder, scroll axes, a separator or a clickable row — so building a typed builder on today's vocabulary would freeze those holes into a compile-checked API. The model correction moved to the new phase F003/P017 (plugin-ui-gaps, 9 tasks). Nobody is working on this task; it resumes once P017 has landed, and then builds the typed builders on a corrected model. Note also that its line \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\" cannot be literally true while the model lives in the app crate — recorded as F003/P017/T9.",
          "description": "Back to planned 2026-07-25: started this session, then split. The research it triggered found that the declarative model cannot express padding, an input placeholder, scroll axes, a separator or a clickable row — so building a typed builder on today's vocabulary would freeze those holes into a compile-checked API. The model correction moved to the new phase F003/P017 (plugin-ui-gaps, 9 tasks). Nobody is working on this task; it resumes once P017 has landed, and then builds the typed builders on a corrected model. Note also that its line \"the WASM SDK re-exports it\" cannot be literally true while the model lives in the app crate — recorded as F003/P017/T9."
        },
        {
          "id": "6c81c18b-1b80-4128-ba2a-276791879edb-check-002-in-progress-blocked",
          "date": "2026-07-27T18:00:04.486Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "blocked",
          "title": "Blocked on F003/P011/T018 (2026-07-27). The inventory taken for this task found that `border` and `glow` cannot be authored at all — a property value is a closed list of scalars with no object, so `Border{color,width}` cannot be written. Building the typed SDK on that would ship an exceptions list saying appearance is partly unreachable, freezing the hole into a compile-checked API — which is the exact reason this task was split out of the phase in 2026-07-25. The user's decision: fix the foundation first. Nothing here is wasted: the decisions and the full inventory (per-widget properties with types, events per kind, which kinds take children, the shared Layout/Visual keys) are recorded in this task's description and stay valid.",
          "description": "Blocked on F003/P011/T018 (2026-07-27). The inventory taken for this task found that `border` and `glow` cannot be authored at all — a property value is a closed list of scalars with no object, so `Border{color,width}` cannot be written. Building the typed SDK on that would ship an exceptions list saying appearance is partly unreachable, freezing the hole into a compile-checked API — which is the exact reason this task was split out of the phase in 2026-07-25. The user's decision: fix the foundation first. Nothing here is wasted: the decisions and the full inventory (per-widget properties with types, events per kind, which kinds take children, the shared Layout/Visual keys) are recorded in this task's description and stay valid."
        },
        {
          "id": "6c81c18b-1b80-4128-ba2a-276791879edb-check-003-blocked-planned",
          "date": "2026-07-27T18:23:31.573Z",
          "fromStatus": "blocked",
          "toStatus": "planned",
          "title": "Unblocked 2026-07-27: both prerequisites shipped. F003/P011/T018 (`f2deecd`) gave property values an object, so `border` and `glow` are authorable and the SDK needs no exceptions list for them. F003/P011/T019 (`1653169`) gave the fixed value sets real types, so the builders can be honestly typed rather than taking strings for orientation, axes, severity, label side, marker, text align and the 52 glyph names.",
          "description": "Unblocked 2026-07-27: both prerequisites shipped. F003/P011/T018 (`f2deecd`) gave property values an object, so `border` and `glow` are authorable and the SDK needs no exceptions list for them. F003/P011/T019 (`1653169`) gave the fixed value sets real types, so the builders can be honestly typed rather than taking strings for orientation, axes, severity, label side, marker, text align and the 52 glyph names."
        }
